{
 "title": "Waterfall",
 "summary": "An anime waterfall: a cylinder without caps scaled into a wide sheet, loop cuts, subdivision, a Musgrave Displace on an empty driven down (#-frame); an emission shader built in layers on the cylinder's UVs: two noises through water-colour ramps flowing down at their own #frame speeds, mixed by a clamped mask; voronoi foam; glossy reflections and diffuse shading through Shader to RGB, clamped and added / multiplied; foam lines from a distorted wave texture whose phase is driven; a falling noise as the alpha mask for a transparent mix. A bigger copy behind with its own material (smaller, sharper alpha, other speeds).",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "Waterfall",
   "description": "the front sheet"
  },
  {
   "name": "Waterfall2",
   "description": "the back sheet"
  }
 ],
 "expected_result": "Two layers of stylized blue water falling, with white foam specks, horizontal foam lines moving down, and gaps where it is transparent.",
